  "limitations": [
    "The audit does not train anything, does not build a student and does not claim the target is learnable.",
    "No downstream task accuracy (CV-Bench or otherwise) is measured or claimed.",
    "No FPGA latency, resource or speedup number is measured or claimed.",
    "The semantic comparator is the existing cached max-over-prompt-token teacher only; no new semantic model is loaded.",
    "The grounding area target and the pointing bilinear target have different structural support (an area over many cells vs at most four cells), so part of the same-image spatial separation reflects that structural difference and not only task-relevant geometry.",
    "Low spatial/semantic agreement means the objectives differ, not automatically that either target is wrong.",
    "The hardware-regular anchor baseline is a descriptive reference over the L2 saliency score in this zero-update audit; it is not a trained selector.",
    "All numbers are TRAIN-split, image-level and CPU float64 internal measurements, never a promotion gate."
  ],
  "notes": {
    "compatibility_definition": "Spearman is between the spatial target and the cached teacher_soft_target; full NDCG uses the spatial target as the ranking score and teacher_soft_target as the graded relevance",
    "decision_rule": "SPATIAL_SUPERVISION_SIGNAL_PRESENT requires all integrity checks to pass and the 95% bootstrap CI lower bound of spatial-semantic to be greater than zero for BOTH JS and TV; top-K results are descriptive only and cannot override this rule",
    "independent_unit": "the independent unit is the image (grounding/pointing are a paired same-image pair, never two independent samples)",
    "learnability_untested": "even if the signal is present, learnability and downstream task accuracy remain untested",
    "no_blending": "the spatial targets are never blended with the semantic teacher target",
    "no_holm": "a single pre-registered family (JS and TV) is reported with raw two-sided p-values; no multiple-comparison correction is invented",
    "train_only": "the split comes from index metadata only and only train feature caches are opened; val/test npz files are never resolved or read",
    "zero_update": "only array math and imported metric helpers are used; no optimizer, no parameter, no checkpoint, no model is created or updated"
  },
